From b14361136b23f71ae207379673a9b4730ef485bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: batya <batya@github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:54:38 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] feat(agent): the answers live with what they are about

"In this session" is kept in the session itself (a `session_agent` row pointing at the
session, so it goes when the session goes), "always" is one switch in the studio's
settings - "let the agent make tracks without asking" - and "never" joins a list of
forbidden tools that no request can talk the studio out of. The table of remembered
permissions is gone: nothing about the person's answers sits in a table of its own.

The window shows the new shape in Settings, Agent (MCP): the leash, the one switch and
the forbidden list, with a cross to forgive a tool. Asking in the window is what makes
the track: with a session open the request carries the same five decisions - once, this
session, always, ask every time, never - and without one the person makes a session or
brings an old one back first. A tool that cannot be undone is never waved through for
good, so its modal has no "always": once, this session, ask every time, never.

The MCP skill says the same, in the words the agent reads, and the whole studio is
checked by the tests (210 passed).
